{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1181363-fanmade-dark-era-leviathan-mage-entwined-dragons","id":1181363,"title":"[Fanmade Dark Era] [Leviathan/Mage] Entwined Dragons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-01T05:31:38-08:00","id":1181363,"title":"[Fanmade Dark Era] [Leviathan/Mage] Entwined Dragons","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\">Hello, people. I am a native Korean who usually talks in Korean RPG forums, which are relatively small. This is my proposal for another Dark Era setting I wrote in on of them. I thought I should share it with Onyx Path forum, since it has much more members and diversity. It is an open project, any contribution or constructive criticism is welcome. Also, my English could contain errors.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\">Entwined Dragons</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Korea, Yeomal Seoncho[\uc5ec\ub9d0\uc120\ucd08, <span style=\"color:#373A3C\">\uf988\u672b\u9bae\u521d, End of Goryeo, Beginning of Joseon]</span>. 1374~1422 AD</span><br /> <br /> Goryeo dynasty is at ruins. Once an independent, strong, and proud nation that defended the Cathay's invasion successfully, Goryeo was forced to kneel at the mighty Mongols after 30 years of war. Since then, Yuan dynasty of Mongol has never stopped meddling. Young women were forced to sent to Yuan to become cocubines, kings were toppled if resistant, and Yuan collaborators turns farmers into their slave by force, intimidation and crimes.<br /> <br /> That was until Gongmin-wang(\uacf5\ubbfc\uc655, <span style=\"color:#373A3C\">\u606d\u610d\u738b, King Gongmin)</span> was enthroned at 1351. Like any other kings, he was married to a Yuan princess Noguk(\ub178\uad6d\ub300\uc7a5\uacf5\uc8fc, <span style=\"color:#373A3C\">\u9b6f\u570b\u5927\u9577\u516c\u4e3b)</span>. But that did not stop them from enacting reforms. Yuan was suffering from Han Chinese rebellions, and Gongmin seized the opportunity. Intervening Yuan officials were banished, collaborators were thrown out from offices, and lost land was reconquered. Reforms were making notable progresses.<br /> <br /> Then the Hong-gunjuk(\ud64d\uac74\uc801, <span style=\"color:#373A3C\">\u7d05\u5dfe\u8cca, R</span>ed Turban Rebels)s came. And the Wae-gu(\uc65c\uad6c, \u502d\u5bc7, Japanese Pirates)s. Because of the corruption and meddling, Goryeo's military strength was barley enough to handle them. The King was forced to flee from capital many times. In the end, Honggunjuk was driven out, and onslaught of Waegu has stopped for a brief moment, but Goryeo lost valuable time for reforms.</span><br /> <br /> The royal couple did not have babies(there were some miscarriages) for a long time, then in 1365 the queen went into labor. Despite Gongmin's frantic attempts to save her, both Noguk and her baby died in childbirth. By losing his true love, only guide and ally, King Gongmin was depraved, but he could not give up his country yet.<br /> <br /> Then Sin Don came. Sin Don was a lowly Buddhist monk. His origin are unknown to this day, but Gongmin trusted him, and granted him absolute power to continue the reforms. Sin Don returned noble's illegally gained farms to rightful owners, freed slave that were once free people, revived the Sung-gyungwan(\uc131\uade0\uad00, <span style=\"color:#373A3C\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">\u6210\u5747\u9928, National </span></span>Confucian College). His methods were straightforward, quick, and effective. Because of this, nobles and powerful families despised him. Neo-Confucian reformists called Shinjin Sadaebu(\uc2e0\uc9c4\uc0ac\ub300\ubd80, <span style=\"color:#373A3C\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">\u65b0\u9032\u58eb\u5927\u592b, New wave scholar-official) </span></span>did not like him because of his background of Buddhist monk. Furthermore, it is said that Sin got lost in power, having mistresses and acquiring fortune. Gongmin also was afraid of Sin's growing power, and he was executed.<br /> <br /> That was the end of reforms. King gave up everything. Some say he went insane. He turned to perverted sexual acts toward both men and women. He ordered his male sex partners to rape his cocubines, and when one of them turned pregnant, he tried to kill them all. Unfortunately, the rapists got him first. Gongmin was brutally murdered in 1374.<br /> <br /> Yi Inim(\uc774\uc778\uc784, \uf9e1<span style=\"color:#373A3C\">\u4ec1\u4efb</span>), a pro-Yuan noble who was the target of the reform(to be fair, he was a reformist in his early days, it was the death of Gongmin that shook him and corrupted him) took over the government. 10 year old Woo, who was Gongmin's only son from Sin Don's housemaid was appointed King. A corrupt but shrewd and effective ruler, Yi Inim negates all reforms, but runs country smoothly without any noise. But still, shadows are creeping from every corner of the country.<br /> <br /> This is the start of Yeomal Seoncho. It is probably the most popular era in Korean History due to its importance and interesting characters. It has been made into historical dramas many times featuring different interpretation each time. It is a time of conflicting ideologies, shining ideals and necessary evils, Korean society was forever changed after this. After Yeomal Seoncho, a golden age of Korea begins by Sejong the Great.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Timeline</span><br /> 1374: Enthronement of Woo.<br /> 1376: Choi Young wins battle against Waegu<br /> 1380: Choi Museon defeats Waegu by using new weapons- cannons.<br /> 1380: Yi Seonggye destroys Waegu army. Organized attacks from Waegu are ended.<br /> 1383: Jung Dojeon meets Yi Seonggye. Jung becomes Yi's most trusted advisor. Many say Jung is the designer of Joseon dynasty.<br /> 1388: Yi Inim is removed from office by Choi Young and Yi Seonggye.<br /> 1388: Choi Young and King Woo order Yi Seonggye to attack Ming China. He refuses and does Coup d'etat.<br /> 1388: Woo is removed from throne, his son Chang becomes king.<br /> 1389: Chang is removed from throne, Yi Seonggye's relative Gongyang becomes king.<br /> 1389~1392: King Gongyang and Jung Mongjoo resists and politically attacks Lee Seonggye and his men. Yi Seonggye's greatest crisis<br /> 1392: Yi Seonggye's son Yi Bangwon orders to kill Jung Mongjoo in broad daylight.<br /> 1392: Yi Seonggye becomes king(Taejo). Goryeo's end. Joseon's beginning.<br /> 1392: Yi Seonggye makes his youngest son Yi Bangseok crown prince.<br /> 1392~1398: Jung Dojeon passes various laws, leading to reforms. Many royal family is enraged, thinking Jung Dojeon is more powerful than the king.<br /> 1398: First Strife of Princes. Yi Bangwon commits coup saying &quot;it is wrong to make a second wife's son heir while firstborn is alive.&quot; He kills Yi Bangseok and his brother Bangbeon, Jung Dojeon and many more. Shocked by his best friend and son's death, Taejo resigns from throne and goes to his northeast hometown. Yi Bang-gwa, then eldest son, becomes king(Jeongjong).<br /> 1400: Second Strife of Princes. Yi Bangwon's elder brother Bang-gan tries coup. Yi Bangwon easily stops this. Yi Bang-gan is spared. Bangwon becomes king(Taejong).<br /> 1402: Rebellion of Jo Saui. This rebellion was supported by Taejo Yi Sunggye. Taejong Yi Bangwon surpresses the rebellion. Taejo admits defeat and returns to palace. It is known that Taejo and Taejong made up later.<br /> 1408: Taejo dies.<br /> 1409: Fearing the meddling from queen's relatives. He purges his two brother-in-law. They are killed a year later.<br /> 1409~1418: Taejong purges his former helpers and lieutenants, none of them were killed. But most are forced into resigns, cast out to frontiers, or moved into just honorary titles.<br /> 1418: Taejong changes crown prince from Yangnyeong to Chungnyeong.<br /> 1418: King Sejong takes the throne. Taejong resigns and becomes High King.<br /> 1419: Taejong purges Sejong's in law. Sejong's father-in-law Sim on is killed, his family made into slaves all except the Queen.<br /> 1422: Taejong dies.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Inspirational Materials<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Veritable Records of the Joseon Dynasty-A official history book renowned for its accuracy and independence from political powers.<br /> Tears of the Dragon-1997 Korean Historical Drama<br /> Jung Dojeon-2014 Korean Historical Drama<br /> Six Flying Dragons-2015 Korean Historical Drama</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> This is all for today. I will be returning with supernaturals, themes, moods. I hope you liked it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23621-tg0098","user":"tg0098","date":".  Fixed some typo/editing 02-02-2018, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23621-tg0098","name":"tg0098","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23621_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T06:28:04-08:00","id":1181375,"title":"","content":"Curious to see how you are going to integrate Leviathan and Mage's themes with this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T00:36:13-08:00","id":1181585,"title":"","content":"How did I miss this thread?! Glad to see another Korean. I'm weak on history, but fare better on CoD.<br /> <br /> I'm surprised you chose Leviathan, since it's a fangame and thus relatively lacking in materials (especially 2E) to work with, and I admit I didn't look closely into Leviathan ever since Beast came out... Was it the dragon imagery?<br /> <br /> Anyways, I look forward to what you have prepared for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T02:37:13-08:00","id":1181600,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:24px\">Supernaturals</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Leviathan: the Tempest</span></span><br /> <br /> &quot;You call me a son of Sin Don, but we Wang families are descendant of dragons! Come here and look.&quot; Onlookers came and saw Woo's armpit gleaming with fish-like scales. It was the most peculiar thing. - Yi Junghwan, 'Taekliji(\ud0dd\ub9ac\uc9c0, \u64c7\u91cc\u5fd7, Determining Advantageous Lands)'<br /> <br /> Past and Future<br /> <br /> It is said that Jak Jegeon, grandfather of the Goryeo's founder Wang Geon, married a daughter of western sea's dragon king. Since then, blood of the dragon flows in Wang family's veins. In order to keep the bloodline pure, early Goryeo kings would marry their relatives. Although this tradition stops by powerful nobles demanding royal marriages with their family, Goryeo's royal family always carried the trace of Tannim Strain. Gongmin is the last royal Leviathan, one that had not been born in a century because of the sea-fearing nature of Yuan.<br /> <br /> Most Leviathans of Goryeo pledge their allegiance to the Wang royal family. In return, they are granted prestige that few could match. They are rulers of rural seaside village who the governors cannot interfere, traditional nobles whose ancestors helped Wang Geon found this great nation, head monks of Buddhist temples which own the local mountains and rivers.<br /> But as always, change of tides sweep the Tribe. Tribe was torn in two because of the Gongmin's reforms. One side said it was necessary, that they have to give up the privileges or Goryeo will crumble. Others argued the king is not respecting the way of the Tribe. Sure, maybe corrupt mortal nobles should be cleaned out, but to do the same on God-Monsters? No, us Leviathans should be the exception.<br /> <br /> The only thing that stopped the civil war was death of Gongmin. Anti-reformist was pleased at Yi Inim's rule, pro-reformists were worried about the future, but they weren't passionate about reform enough to give up their privileges when no one is asking them to. But history marches on as generals start to gain fame from defeating invaders, and more and more Shinjin Sadaebu s are gathering for revolution, seeing no hope in current regime.<br /> <br /> Once Yi Sunggye's coup succeeds, the Tribe is forced to choose. Will you stay royal to the king, risking your own life? Are you going to collaborate with Yi, to ensure some of the Tribe will survive to next dynasty? Or will you choose the third path, betraying some of the kings but saving the nation? Perhaps is there fourth, or fifth way? The reforms are getting more drastic, stripping many powers that Tribe enjoyed for centuries. It is becoming clear that Neo-Confucianists don't just want some government posts. They want to remake this nation completely, and Leviathans aren't part of it. <br /> <br /> The fall of Leviathans begins with Joseon. The country forges Sain geom(\uc0ac\uc778\uac80, \u56db\u5bc5\u528d, Four tiger sword), a blade that is only made on tiger year, tiger month, tiger day, tiger hour which fills it with pure Yang. Used correctly, sain geom surges with electrical power, making it deadly bane for Leviathans. The new government organizes hunters to locate and kill the Tribe. Many lives will be lost, including the collaborators who were promised safety in return. After Taejong is inaugurated, the hunt stops and remaining ones are officially pardoned. But Leviathans will continued to be persecuted through Joseon dynasty.<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> I should probably write strains and schools, but got lost in ideas. Do you think all strains and schools should include Korean names for them? There aren't a lot of sea monsters or gods in Chinese&amp;Korean mythology so I could use some help with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23621-tg0098","name":"tg0098","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23621_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T02:41:24-08:00","id":1181601,"title":"","content":"This looks very promising and it's focused on a time window I know little about. Will keep an eye on this, it does seem interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T02:48:53-08:00","id":1181603,"title":"","content":"Considering what the Wake does to people, this says some... <i>interesting </i>things about the general mental state of the royalty and the higher nobility, as well as the country itself.<br /> <br /> There are seven Strains, right? Buddhist lore mentions eight &quot;dragon kings,&quot; i.e. Naga Raja. Maybe you can have seven of them as the Strains' names? Buddhist culture did flourish in Goryeo, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T03:30:45-08:00","id":1181611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1181363-fanmade-dark-era-leviathan-mage-entwined-dragons?p=1181601#post1181601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This looks very promising and it's focused on a time window I know little about. Will keep an eye on this, it does seem interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for your interest. I really enjoyed your &quot;The Forest that Weeps&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1181363-fanmade-dark-era-leviathan-mage-entwined-dragons?p=1181603#post1181603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering what the Wake does to people, this says some... <i>interesting </i>things about the general mental state of the royalty and the higher nobility, as well as the country itself.<br /> <br /> There are seven Strains, right? Buddhist lore mentions eight &quot;dragon kings,&quot; i.e. Naga Raja. Maybe you can have seven of them as the Strains' names? Buddhist culture did flourish in Goryeo, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really good idea. I thought about borrowing Yongsaengguja(9 sons of dragons) for Lahmasu's name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23621-tg0098","name":"tg0098","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23621_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T03:37:27-08:00","id":1181612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tg0098</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1181363-fanmade-dark-era-leviathan-mage-entwined-dragons?p=1181611#post1181611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's a really good idea. I thought about borrowing Yongsaengguja(9 sons of dragons) for Lahmasu's name.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can always use the Nine Children for Hybrids in Leviathan. Or perhaps entirely different mythic beings for Mage, like cryptids and spirits.<br /> <br /> Alternatively... Proximi in the Alexandrian age were thought to be descended from Classic heroes. What if Proximi in Asia were thought to be of draconic descent? (Hey, DnD got away with it with their sorcerers...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T05:01:52-08:00","id":1181620,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">Strains and School</span><br /> <br /> Leviathans are a dying race even in Goryeo dynasty. There are estimated a hundred Leviathans in Korean peninsula, not counting Lahmasus. In Korea, Leviathans call themselves Haesoo(\ud574\uc218, \u6d77\u7378, sea monsters), which could be also read as harmful monsters. Since Korea have a vary diverse nautical ecosystem, there are no sea life could not be manifested in Leviathan's forms.<br /> <br /> Strains are called Jipa(\uc9c0\ud30c) in Korea. The Lahmasu's names are originated from Yongsaengguza(\uc6a9\uc0dd\uad6c\uc790, \uf9c4\u751f\u4e5d\u5b50, Nine sons of Dragon). Strain somewhat defines how do you feel about this moment. The exceptions are there, but usually the same strain shares the same attitude.<br /> <br /> The Bahamutans call themselves Gon(\uace4), which is a giant whale appearing in Zhuangzi's book. They are most gentle and caring strain, usually landlords, and tend to stay in local regions albeit not too far from capital. They make their cult self-sufficient, emphasizing on farming and fishing, and do not care for politics or reforms. This is tradition, and they will continue to keep it no matter what happens. Their Lahmasu's name is Bihui(\ube44\ud76c)<br /> <br /> The Dagonites call themselves Agwi(\uc544\uadc0), name for big mouth fish. They are most numerous among the Korean Leviathans. They make their cult in very secluded areas like small islands, and do not care for neither Confucianism nor Buddhism. Aside from Tannim, Dagonites are least favorable toward Joseon, not because of their loyalty, but because they oppose Joseon\u2019s policy of centralization. Their Lahmasu's name is Docheol(\ub3c4\ucca0).<br /> <br /> The Lahamins call themselves Chodo(\ucd08\ub3c4), a monster that likes to lock things. Many Lahamins form a cult that is considered heretical to most Buddhist. Like cult of Mireuk(\ubbf8\ub975, a future Buddha who will come and fix all the problems in the world). They frequently enjoy this chaos, since this gives them more followers. They name their Lahmasu Heonjang(\ud5cc\uc7a5).<br /> <br /> The Nus call themselves Hondon(\ud63c\ub3c8), primordial monster of chaos itself. Despite its name, Nu are probably the most mainstream strain. It isn\u2019t numerous, but it has no problem joining Buddhists or Confucianists, studying scripture and practicing belief. Cults think of themselves as followers and disciples. They are the ones who is obsessed about making a jokbo(\uc871\ubcf4, family tree) for all tribe. Their Lahmasu is known as Gongbok(\uacf5\ubcf5).<br /> <br /> The Oceanids call themselves Shinjikki(\uc2e0\uc9c0\ub07c), mermaid goddess of the sea. They are the ones who stay in capital and make political factions. The most powerful and prosperous Strain, they are known for perversion and many marriages. They remain fairly neutral about Joseon. It is just another opportunity like always. They have survived the Mongols, surely they can get through this. The problem is, they are the most hated Leviathans to the Shinjin Sadaebu. Their Lahmasu is known as Gyo(\uad50).<br /> <br /> The Tannim call themselves Yong(\uc6a9), the dragon itself. Every Tannim in Korea is Wang family, through birth or by giving Wang surname to her. They are the most loyal Strain to Goryeo. That doesn\u2019t mean they are counter reformists, as you can reform without changing the dynasty. But they are ready to throw their lives to stop the usurper. Their Lahmasu is known as Yimoogi(\uc774\ubb34\uae30).<br /> <br /> The Thassalans call themselves Tam(\ud0d0), endless hunger. Once prosperous due to active foreign trade policy of Goryeo, they are struggling these times. When China, Korea, Japan are all in civil war or chaos, it\u2019s hard to make money through trade. Nevertheless, they are contacting with various regimes to ensure their profit. They do not like Neo Confucianists, since they think merchant are lowly class who produce nothing and only exploits, but are eager to set deals with the new regime. Their Lahmasu is known as Suwoo(\uc218\uc6b0).<br /> <br /> Schools are called Hakdang(\ud559\ub2f9, \u5b78\u7576) in Korea. Schools represent how you react to problems. Of course, having the same problem makes it easier to look for same solutions, but not always. There is no School of Sand, and School of Clay got split into two.<br /> <br /> Dowon Hakdang(\ub3c4\uc6d0\ud559\ub2f9), the School of Abyss tries to retreat to Dowon(\ub3c4\uc6d0, \u6843\u5712, Peach garden), which is a island far away in ocean, an ideal place for Leviathans to live in. This school tries to solve problem by cutting all contacts with human society. This is somewhat different from western School of Abyss, which views sea as their final resting place and not an island.<br /> <br /> Juja Hakdang(\uc8fc\uc790\ud559\ub2f9), the first School of Clay borrows its name from creator of Neo Confucianism Zhu Xi(Korean name Juhui, or in reverence, Juja). Since this philosophy-religion teaches its followers everyone can become a gentleman, Malkut\u2019s believe they, even if monsters and gods, could clean their body and fix this county\u2019s problems. If you are using only English name, call it \u201cSchool of Bamboo.\u201d<br /> <br /> Bulbub Hakdang(\ubd88\ubc95\ud559\ub2f9), the second School of Clay believes in Buddhism sincerely. There are many stories of Buddha turning his attention towards lowly beasts, saying every creature lies a fracture of Buddha, and has the chance to become enlightened. Dragons and Nagas became protector of Dharma. So why shouldn\u2019t we? If you are using only English name, call it \u201cSchool of Lotus.\u201d<br /> <br /> Murim Hakdang(\ubb34\ub9bc\ud559\ub2f9), the School of Fog are hostile towards its enemies, especially Yi Sunggye and his followers. They say Tribe should unite and fight with the warlord. Having keen interest in the new weapons, they are trying to control Hwayakguk(\ud654\uc57d\uad6d, Department of Gunpowder).<br /> <br /> Bango Hakdang(\ubc18\uace0\ud559\ub2f9), the School of Moon reveres Bango, a Giant who willingly sacrifice himself to create the world as their creator. They contact other countries and gather information, believing that if they could figure out how Bango created this world, they could do the same with a new nation.<br /> <br /> Dangun Hakdang(\ub2e8\uad70\ud559\ub2f9), the School of Sun\u2019s Korean name comes from Dangun, title of a legendary priest-king from the first Korean nation. They believe by expanding cults and eventually seizing the government, they could rule like Dangun did.<br /> <br /> <br /> Living as Leviathan in Goryeo is easy and comfortable, but it is constantly anxious. This is why the Tribe is forming Cohorts more than ever before. To solve the countries problem and confirm their survival. In Joseon, Cohorts are not choice, but necessity if you do not want to get killed by hunters.<br /> My default option about Leviathan Chronicle is that it will be a tragedy. Joseon will be born, Tribe will be on the verge of extinction, if you are lucky you might get to survive until Taejong's pardons, which most don't.<br /> <br /> In Entwined Dragons, Leviathans reflect people who were at the wrong place at the wrong time, more specifically, a good man who benefited from corrupt systems and didn't think much about it. Sure, we could blame them for some mistakes and selfishness, but in reality, they were ordinary people. Woo\u2019s only fault was that he wasn\u2019t a skilled ruler. Chang\u2019s only fault was that the 7 year old was Woo\u2019s son. But in Joseon\u2019s perspective, they had to be killed. Their existence itself was a threat to the new nation. The same could be said with some nobles and Buddhists who were mercilessly persecuted in Joseon era. In western history, Louis XVI and Marie Antoinette are somewhat of a good example. Yes, they were part of the \u201cAncien Regime\u201d, they did take profits from people\u2019s pain. But did they deserve it? Well, maybe the best answer is for the success of the reform and new system, some collateral damage are unavoidable.<br /> <br /> This will be further explained when I write about theme and mood. Next time, I will be returning with Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23621-tg0098","user":"tg0098","date":".  OK. The editing was horrible. Added some new stuff. 02-02-2018, 08:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23621-tg0098","name":"tg0098","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23621_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T23:16:51-08:00","id":1181923,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\">Mage: the Awakening</span><br /> <br /> <i>While determining the new capital's boundaries, there was an argument between monk Muhak, a mentor of Taejo, and Jung Dojeon, Taejo\u2019s best advisor. According to Pungsu(\ud48d\uc218, \u98a8\u6c34, Feng Shi) if the Seon rock was inside the capital boundary, Buddhism would flourish, if outside, Confucianism will flourish instead. Muhak believed in Pungsu, and wanted to put Seon rock inside. Jung Dojeon thought it was nonsense, and wanted to put it outside for practical reasons. Taejo stopped the argument, saying they should decide it tomorrow. It was snowing that night, and when morning came, only the snow outside Seon rock was melted. Seeing it as omen, Taejo decided to put it outside the capital walls. Muhak cried out loud. &quot;Alas! Is it fate? Is it heavens will? We monks will be little more than slaves for five hundred years.&quot; - Folklore of Seoul</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Past and Future</span></span><br /> Korea always had a rich tradition of magic. Shamans serving pagan gods and spirits who could bring rain and cure diseases, Buddhist monks who could read destinies and compel evil spirits, skilled craftsmen forging magical flutes to harness ocean and drive away invaders, they were the mages of Korea. They were always close to society, but not in politics. They obeyed king's orders, but never did they tried to interfere in the matters of the state.<br /> <br /> This time, it is different. Neo-Confucianism teaches that principles of universe, morality of individuals, governing of nations are not separated. Awakened who are motivated by it plan grand schemes, both in magic and mundane, trying to change Goryeo. They use spells to further their mortal ideologies, and use mundane politics to complete their supernal plan. Mages who don't want to meddle in Fallen World's affairs have no choice but to step in and stop their colleagues.<br /> <br /> During Yi Inim's rule, many Awakened wander to find their patron, be it a young king who is desperate to be freed from Yi Inim's shackles, a local landlord who is known to be generous, a famous general renowned for his martial prowess. This is the time when many foreign elements are flooding into Goreyo, Neo-Confucianism is the most important, but there are many more, like Taoist alchemy, Japanese Shinto, Mongolian Tengri religion. Some try to find the answers hidden in the lost history of Korea. This is the time for preparation, sharpening your ideologies and earning trust of your patron.<br /> <br /> Yi Sunggye's coup divides Mages, especially those who believe in Neo Confucianism. Many view it as heretical, clear opposite of what Confucius said of loyalty and duty, others view it as prime example of revolution theory of Mencius. As the debate continues, many will be shocked to find how their ideologies differ, when they thought they were sharing the same ideal. These will often result in violence and purges, as lifelong friends tries to kill each other. Buddhists and other Awakened are no different when it comes to infighting, since it is clear the new dynasty will bring change of cultures. In the end, everyone is forced to take a side. You can't be neutral on a moving train.<br /> <br /> These fights will continue to end until death of Taejong, after that it is clear who are the winner of this ideological and cultural warfare. Mages who built Joseon will face witch hunt and purges, since to Yi Bangwon, they have outlived their usefulness. Jung Dojeon's death is a clear example of this. Even if you help Yi Bangwon to become Taejong by betraying some of your ideals, your fate could be no different. But Mages are more hopeful than Leviathans, since pupils of the fallen will continue to teach and educate the young, they will rise once more. Whether or not this is a good thing to Korea, none can tell.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Orders and Paths</span><br /> There are many mages in Korea with various magical traditions. Since Goryeo dynasty occasionally traded with Arab and Southeast Asian countries, some mages practice truly esoteric ways. Koreans call the Atlantis Ju(\uc8fc, \u5468, Zhou), an ancient kingdom of China that all confucians idealized. As one could easily translate both Mage(\uc220\uc0ac, Sulsa), and names of the Orders(Silver Ladders came from Platonic origin, so they are called differently). I will only note names of the Paths.<br /> <br /> There are five Orders in Korea. Orders all called Gyeolsa(\uacb0\uc0ac, \u7d50\u793e).<br /> The Adamantine Arrow, like always train martial arts and weaponry. People of Korea a long known for their archery skills, so their are many sharpshooters in the Order. Talons typically fought against the Honggeonjeoks and Waegus, and will participate in short civil wars. They also act as wandering gosu(\uace0\uc218), a skilled person, and stops corrupt nobles from exploiting the weak. Few even become bandits, either working only for their own gain, or helping poor people by stealing from the rich.<br /> <br /> The Guardians of the Veil are hesitant about today's situations. Too many Mages are using their power without caution. But some of them are active participants of the revolution, since Joseon dynasty aims for meritocracy, and are not afraid to commit necessary evils. The Order approaches social pariahs such as beggars, gisaeng(\uae30\uc0dd, female performers), and butchers, and have made those people work in Gaebang(\uac1c\ubc29) in order to collect information and to spy on the powerful.<br /> <br /> The Mysterium is mostly unconcerned and focuses on preserving and guarding knowledge from era of chaos. They are leaned towards Neo Confucianism, since they value knowledge and records more than anything, but they are also afraid of its puritan nature. Mysterium values every knowledge, including Buddhism, heretical philosophies from warring states period, and pagan religion. Neo Confucian don't burn those books, but they shun preserving them. Another mission of the Order is to maintain contact with other country's Awakened, and share each other's knowledge.<br /> <br /> The Silver Ladders is called Gentleman Society(\uad70\uc790\ud68c, \u541b\u5b50\u6703). They are the main participants at Yeomal Seoncho era. Most of them join the political factions, trying to make the world Ju once more. They tries to bring the Diamonds into politics, believing they should work together to achieve victory. They also tries to recruit Nameless Mages in the name of enlightenment and humanitarianism. Almost every single Theraches believe in Neo Confucianism, though the exact opinion, especially on accepting Buddhism and changing dynasty varies from person to person.<br /> <br /> The Nameless are mostly consisted of commoners and foreigners. They are cynical about the Diamonds, saying they don't represent true people. Although they will admit some of the reforms made life better, they also think little about revolution and political debates. Nameless mages typically tries to make their own rules in small communities, where everyone could live without fear of death, starvation, and violence.<br /> <br /> Surprisingly, Seers of the Throne, who are the corrupt and sadistic nobles of Goryeo, are quiet neutral about the revolution. They are not enthusiastic since they know the reforms could strip their powers and privileges, but they sense the tension between the Yi family and the Neo Confucian. By flattery and submission, Seers are positive they can turn the tide against the Diamonds. Even if the new dynasty begins, Seers of the Throne will be victorious in the end.<br /> <br /> These are the five paths of Korea. Paths are called Bubdo(\ubc95\ub3c4, \u6cd5\u9053).<br /> Acanthus are called Geukto(\uadf9\ud1a0, \u68d8\u571f, thorny earth). They are a Gwansangjaengyi(\uad00\uc0c1\uc7c1\uc774, Facelookers) who warns people of ill omens, a Buddhists monk who are well versed in accidents and inevitability, a trainee who wants to become Shinseon(\uc2e0\uc120, \u795e\u4ed9, a person who gained immortality) by being freed from time. Though shunned by scholar-officials, many royals and nobles come looking for witches for their advise, either to find comfort or to prepare for danger. It is said that Yi Sunggye himself visited facelookers many times. Enchanters are very few, but continued its legacy throughout the dynasty.<br /> <br /> Mastigos are called Yeoksoo(\uc5ed\uc218, \u75ab\u6c34, scourging water). They are a scholar who studied Jonghwengga(\uc885\ud6a1\uac00, \u7e31\u6a6b\u5bb6, a philosophical school in Warring States period that focuses on diplomacy) and could move peoples mind by simple words, a practicer of Pungsu who could predict nation's future by looking at king's tombs, a gosu who could climb entire mountains by blink of an eye. They use trickery and deception to get what they want. Warlocks and Psychopomps were both valued even in Joseon, although some puritan scholars rejected them.<br /> <br /> Moros are called Pilgeum(\ud544\uae08, \u5fc5\uf90a, inevitable metal). They are a confucian who have mastered the five elements, a merchant who studies both Arabic and Taoist alchemy, a governor who just listens to ghost's stories and persuades them to leave the earth. Korea had a tradition of honoring ancestors, and it was amplified by the introduction of Confucianism. Officially, Confucianism reject ghosts, saying they are only honoring them because it is proper manners to do so. Necromancers flourished, although in half-ignored way, in both Goryeo and Joseon, Alchemists were treated less and only understanding, never practicing, of elements were encouraged.<br /> <br /> Obrimos are called Bunhwa(\ubd84\ud654, \u61a4\u706b, raging fire). They are a devout Neo-Confucian who studies the principle of the universe, a pro-Yuan noble who secretly practices Tengri religion, a soldier who chants simple spells that could deflect arrows. It is the most venerated path in Yeomal Seoncho, because of its connection to Neo Confucianism. They try to fix Goryeo by changing the connections between the Prime and people. Force Arcanum is looked down upon, and only used practically.<br /> <br /> Thyrsus are called Yumok(\uc720\ubaa9, \u904a\u6728, playful wood). They are a medic who uses acupuncture to fix people's diseases, a mudang(\ubb34\ub2f9, shaman) who worships spirit of the mountain, a local landlord using rituals to make the crops grow faster. Because Korea was always an agricultural state, Ecstatics were always welcomed, and government brought a lot of effort into increasing the skills of farmers and medics. Shamans on the other hand, are indeed treated as pariahs, although sometimes the nation officially give rites to major spirits.<br /> <br /> In Entwined Dragons, Mages represent self-righteous interllectuals who want to change the world. Jung Mongju, Jung Dojeon are most famous examples. Once lifelong friends, Jung Mongju tried to execute Jung Dojeon in order to save Goryeo dynasty, Jung Dojeon was saved because Yi Bangwon killed Mongju in a nick of time. Jung Dojeon became the top Vizier and tried to make Joseon a state where King and his subjects ruled together, but killed by Yi Bangwon, who thought power of the kings are more important.<br /> <br /> Confucianism heavily emphasizes on intellectual\u2019s responsibilities. If a person is learned, she shouldn\u2019t be satisfied with herself. She should do her best trying to make the world a better place, even if it means die trying. In Neo Confucianism, more so. Countless Scholar-Officials of China and Korea tried their best to save the people.<br /> But to do that, compromise is necessary. You could be forced to harm innocent people whose only sin was not agreeing with you. Many Confucians became corrupted, or used as pawns of powers that be. Worse, maybe history will judge you as nothing more than well intended extremist who stopped progress and started a dark era.<br /> These will be further explored in themes and moods, which I will write next time.<br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23621-tg0098","user":"tg0098","date":".  Got the names of the Paths. Thanks a lot. 02-03-2018, 08:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23621-tg0098","name":"tg0098","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23621_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T23:42:33-08:00","id":1181927,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d assign the Five Energies (Wu Xing) to the Paths\u2019 names, like how Hellenistic mages named themselves after the Classical elements, and Kemetic mages after the five-part soul. Taoist and Confucian mages would especially identify themselves with the Wu Xing, while Buddhist mages follow the five tattva (basically same stuff as the Classic elements, but with akasha instead of ether). <br /> <br /> In fact, here\u2019s what I had in mind, separate from yours. By all means please do take them apart for anything you can salvage from them. (Since they hardly fit with any of the nicknames you already have in mind for them)<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> The Path of Wood resonate with the direction of east, the virtue of compassion, and the color green. The Blue Dragons walk in the sylvan mountains, honoring its gods and binding beast-demons.<br /> <br /> The Path of Fire resonate with the direction of south, the virtue of propriety, and the color red. The Vermillion Sparrows walk in the five-day markets, striking bargains that warm when fulfilled but burn when broken. <br /> <br /> The Path of Earth resonate with the direction of center, the virtue of trust, and the color yellow. The Yellow Snakes walk among both rising powers and fallen graces, unshakable in their conviction over both society and nature. <br /> <br /> The Path of Metal resonate with the direction of west, the virtue of honor, and the color white. The White Tigers walk in bloody battlefields and ravaged countrysides, confronting human failings so that they may rise above them. <br /> <br /> The Path of Water resonate with the direction of north, the virtue of prudence, and the color black. The Black Turtles walk in the desolate and uncanny places of the world, speaking to things that which ought not be alive.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 02-03-2018, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T05:35:00-08:00","id":1181971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tg0098</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1181363-fanmade-dark-era-leviathan-mage-entwined-dragons?p=1181923#post1181923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As one could easily translate both Mage(\uc220\uc0ac, Sulsa), and names of the Orders, I will only note names of the Paths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does Mysterium translate easily? I mean, it's already the one Order whose name isn't translated because it's a highly specific Latin word.<br /> <br /> Also, how much sense does 'Silver Ladder' make in this period? I mean, it's a direct reference to the Great Chain of Being from Platonism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I didn't decide what to call each paths, do you guys have any idea what each path's name means? </div> </div> </div>They're mostly in To The Strongest.<br /> <br /> A Thyrsus is a short stick with a pine cone on it. It's associated with Dionysus and the Mystery religions devoted to him.<br /> <br /> Moros is a Classical Greek embodiment of Destiny/Doom/ the inevitability of death.<br /> <br /> Acanthus comes from a Classical Greek word for 'thorns/thorny'.<br /> <br /> Obrimos comes from a Classical Greek word for 'Raging One'. It might have slightly more complex implications.<br /> <br /> Mastigos seems to mean something like 'scourge' or 'punishment'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T06:08:15-08:00","id":1181977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1181363-fanmade-dark-era-leviathan-mage-entwined-dragons?p=1181971#post1181971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does Mysterium translate easily? I mean, it's already the one Order whose name isn't translated because it's a highly specific Latin word.<br /> <br /> Also, how much sense does 'Silver Ladder' make in this period? I mean, it's a direct reference to the Great Chain of Being from Platonism.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Japanese players translated Mysterium to Hiouden, I don't know its Chinese characters. If I knew, I could translate it from Sino-Japanese to Sino-Korean. I myself used &quot;Shinbidang(\uc2e0\ube44\ub2f9, \u795e\u79d8\u9ee8, Mystery Party)&quot; when introducing MtAw to Korean players. And you're right. Silver Ladder doesn't fit to this era. How about &quot;Gentlemen society(\uad70\uc790\ud68c, \u541b\u5b50\u6703)&quot; ? Since the term &quot;Gentlemen&quot; both apply to a person born with status of nobility and a person who made himself eminent by training.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1181363-fanmade-dark-era-leviathan-mage-entwined-dragons?p=1181971#post1181971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're mostly in To The Strongest.<br /> <br /> A Thyrsus is a short stick with a pine cone on it. It's associated with Dionysus and the Mystery religions devoted to him.<br /> <br /> Moros is a Classical Greek embodiment of Destiny/Doom/ the inevitability of death.<br /> <br /> Acanthus comes from a Classical Greek word for 'thorns/thorny'.<br /> <br /> Obrimos comes from a Classical Greek word for 'Raging One'. It might have slightly more complex implications.<br /> <br /> Mastigos seems to mean something like 'scourge' or 'punishment'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I will think about it. Or perhaps I should name them after where they were awakened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23621-tg0098","name":"tg0098","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23621_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T17:19:43-08:00","id":1182123,"title":"","content":"Thanks to Micheal and 21C Hermit, I used both of their contributions. Paths are now named after five element+origin of Greek names.<br /> Acanthus is Geukto(\uadf9\ud1a0, \u68d8\u571f, thorny earth, could also mean heavenly land).<br /> Mastigos is Yeoksoo(\uc5ed\uc218, \u75ab\u6c34, scourging water, could also mean head of rebels).<br /> Moros is Pilgeum(\ud544\uae08, \u5fc5\uf90a, inevitable metal, could also mean absolutely forbidden).<br /> Obrimos is Bunhwa(\ubd84\ud654, \u61a4\u706b, raging fire, could also mean eruption).<br /> Thyrsus is Yumok(\uc720\ubaa9, \u904a\u6728, playful wood, could also mean nomad).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23621-tg0098","name":"tg0098","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23621_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T19:01:30-08:00","id":1182147,"title":"","content":"Theme: Necessary Acts<br /> <i>&quot;I will carry all the evil deeds with me. Your majesty, please become a benevolent king.&quot; - Taejong to Sejong, Veritable Records of Joseon Dynasty<br /> &quot;If I had died earlier, my name would be honored. But still, I will do what I must do.&quot; - Jung Dojeon to Taejo, Sambongjib(\uc0bc\ubd09\uc9d1)</i><br /> <br /> In times of chaos, you cannot do what is right, only what is necessary. There are few innocent people in Yeomal Seoncho era.<br /> King Gongmin executed his generals, who saved his country from countless invasion, fearing they would cause rebellion.<br /> Choi Young, a solemn guardian of Goryeo who is known to &quot;look gold as if it were stone&quot;, turned a blind eye on corrupt Yi Inim.<br /> Jung Mongju, a person of &quot;unmatched integrity and morality&quot;, a final loyalist of Goryeo, fabricated false claims and resorted to calumny to ensure survival of Goryeo dynasty.<br /> Jung Dojeon, who always said &quot;the king solely exists because of its people&quot;, ordered a genocide of the Wang family, and tried to kill pardoned politicians with torture.<br /> Yi Bangwon is a perfect example of this. Modern historians view him as a wise and generous king to his people, building the foundation of Joseon, but he killed many enemies, including his brothers, in-laws, and Jung Mongju and Jung Dojeon who were like uncle to him.<br /> <br /> Everyone's excuse is the same: &quot;I did what I had to.&quot; It is true. The tragedy of this era, is that everyone had a point, either by Neo Confucian standards, or today's standards. Yi Bangwon was a final victor of this era, and it is true his vision was successful, but maybe Jung Mongju or Jung Dojeon's plan was also valid. But in order to make them work, violence is necessary.<br /> <br /> Player Characters, either Leviathan or Mage or something else, will face the same dilemma. Keeping your hands clean will mean none of Korea's problems is going to change, fixing problems will mean putting your integrity at risk.<br /> <br /> Mood: Transition<br /> There are many political upheavals in Korean history, but the reason Yeomal Seoncho is so famous is that it isn't just about changing kings. It is the first full scale ideological and cultural warfare in recorded Korean history. Goryeo put equal emphasis on Buddhism, Confucianism, and pagan Korean mythologies, the power of local aristocrats were powerful, culture was decadent and luxurious. While Joseon was pure Neo Confucian state, focused on absolute centralization, and treated simple and clean life as best. Of course, it doesn't change by the nick of time, but tendency is very clear. Joseon will slowly but steadily become the country its founders dreamed of(though some changes were made here and there).<br /> <br /> Player Characters will be the participants of this great transition, whether they think it is good or bad, they must act. Either in order to secure victory for the people, or to stop this totalitarian madness happening. Storytellers are advised to show both side's pros and cons. Goryeo is harmonious but in overall, more corrupt. Joseon is intolerant but cares more for the common people. It is best not to vilify one side.<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> I think this is the end of introductory phase. What do you want to see? Sample characters? Life on Yeomal Seoncho era? Important historical figures? Other supernaturals? Just let me know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23621-tg0098","name":"tg0098","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23621_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T20:29:05-08:00","id":1182159,"title":"","content":"While my vote is for the supernaturals in the peninsula, others might find important historical figures and events, and life in the era more compelling, since this isn't exactly a well-known era/culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T02:07:59-08:00","id":1182205,"title":"","content":"I'm curious about what life in this era is like. Like, an idea of how urbanised the culture is, or how the society is organised on the local level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T15:11:12-08:00","id":1182403,"title":"","content":"never mind","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T06:20:49-08:00","id":1182572,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\">Life in Yeomal Seoncho Era. Part 1</span><br /> This was a time of rapid transition. End of Goryeo was filled with invasion, corruption and starvation, while Beginning of Joseon indeed brought many reforms, including redistribution of lands for the peasants, powerful armies and cleansed politics. Of course, this changes did not happen at once. It took nearly 100 years. So in this section, I will divide every part with things they have in common, then Goryeo and Joseon. I will not question basic systems of this era. The ideal of nation as a centralized collection of self-sustained small communities has its flaws, some of them fatal,<br /> but this is not a history criticism.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Local life and rulers</span><br /> Medieval Korea is an agricultural nation. Vast majority of population are farmers who grows rice, millet, and beans. Crops like potatoes, red pepper, and tobacco has not yet been imported to Korea. Both men and women contribute to farming, although men do more hard work, and women typically engage in secondary business like weaving. Trade is very primitive, and despite many attempts to make an official metal currency, Korea's de facto currency is rice. There are one or two markets in each city, but most of them don't import or export goods to other cities, so many regions are self-sustained. Most of the trading in rural towns are barters. Local nobles fulfill their exotic needs by presents, sometimes working also as bribes. Trading presents will be the main part of nobility's economic system until 17th Century, when advanced markets will emerge.<br /> <br /> End of Goryeo<br /> Although the government sends governors to each provinces, their powers are limited and only acts as military leaders. The local aristocrat families own vast lands acquired by both legal and illegal means, essentially making their own fiefdoms. Many farmers farm by borrowing their lands, in return, they have to pay a percentage of their earnings to the landlord. This semi-taxation rate is insanely high, and many peasants willingly turn themselves into slaves of the nobles. Others leave their homes, becoming wanderers, beggars, laborers and even bandits.<br /> Eventually, local landlords will even make private armies.<br /> <br /> Start of Joseon<br /> Because of the reforms lands will be granted to commoners, many becoming self-employed farmers. The government sends magistrates to each town, and their powers are indeed absolute except superiors, Ombundsmans, and censors which are all from central government. Local nobles will become little more than servitors of the magistrates, although some successfully participates in central politics and retains its local powers. It would be a lie to say all of these magistrates were full of integrity. Since Joseon exempted its ruling class from taxes, in return they were paid with very little wages, barely enough to survive, let alone to maintain dignity. So many of them did took some &quot;gifts&quot; from local citizens. However the corruption was bearable, and there were moral officers who would not touch the peasants even when their family was starving.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Central Govenment</span><br /> As East Asian political system abandoned feudalism long time ago, there are no such things as barons and counts. Only the central government, which is ruled by the king, has absolute power. There are two ways to get a post at the government, one is passing the national examination, the other is called Eumseo(\uc74c\uc11c), which is by having a high raking officer as your brother, father, uncle, grandfather, or father-in-law, although in this way, your maximum position is limited. There are few things learned men can do beside applying for civil service, so many people study hard for exams. This is a tradition that still defines Korea today.<br /> <br /> End of Goryeo. Capital City: Gaegyung(Now Gaeseong, North Korea)<br /> After being defeated by the Mongols, there appeared two another ways to get a post: Flattery to the Yuan dynasty, and bribing your way to it. King Gongmin's reform somewhat made it impossible, but still their are many unsuited officials in this era. As chaos reigns, King Woo, Chang, and Gongyang was powerless, and government was ruled by few powerful men, the first being Yi Inim, the second being Yi Sunggye. Governmental system are a mess, filled with temporary offices made permenant.<br /> <br /> Start of Joseon. Capital City: Hanseong(Now Seoul, South Korea)<br /> National examination is highly praised, and Eumseo is limited to father and grandfather and is disdained among officials. Systems are redefined elegantly. The government is split into three major bodies, Uijeongbu(\uc758\uc815\ubd80, Discussing and Deciding Department), where three chancellors decide the general policy of the nation, and Yukjo(\uc721\uc870, Six Ministries), where public servants execute those policies, and Samsa(\uc0bc\uc0ac, Three Offices) where young censors, inspectors, and advisers freely criticize those policies and officials. The king oversees everything, and tell his subjects his thoughts as final say resides with him, but cannot force his opinion since that would result in criticism and complaints. A national historian records everything, and once a king dies, those memos are made into Veritable Records, which the king is absolutely forbidden to look, and only his subjects can search for it on special occasions.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Academics, Religion, and Philosophy.</span><br /> Academics is highly encouraged in Korea, as Confucius said, it is learning that makes other virtues worthwhile. Poetry and painting, writing essays(but never novels) and enjoying music and nature are considered basic accomplishments of the nobility. Science is advanced, making very accurate calendars and calculating eclipses bypassing medieval Europe. But lack theories and experiments, making it just tools of trade. Buddhism in Korea is Mahayana Buddhism, a sect that focuses on working towards benefits of everyone, not only people who are trying to become Buddha. Neo Confucianism starts to spread. What is Neo Confucianism exactly? Well, Confucianism is just basic ethics. Be loyal for your lord, be kind to people, study and practice, etc. Neo Confucianism adds metaphysics to it, explaining how principle of the universe becomes mandate of heaven. Korean mythology, although lacking central belief system, is widely spread. Buddhist temples accepting some of its deities.<br /> <br /> End of Goryeo.<br /> Buddhism is very prominent, Gaegyung has more than 400 temples in its area. However, temples are as corrupt as local landlords, owning mountains and rivers, lending food by extremely high interests to poor farmers. Neo Confucianism is studied, but is not yet state religion. The nation accepts pagan religion too, as governors duty was to visit holy sites of Korean mythology and perform rituals.<br /> <br /> Start of Joseon.<br /> Buddhism and Korean Mythology is persecuted, calling it &quot;mere superstition&quot;. Jung Dojeon wrote on his book 'Ravings of Buddhism(\ubd88\uc528\uc7a1\ubcc0)': [A foolish monk says &quot;If there are no hell, how can we stop people from being evil?&quot;. I answer &quot;A gentlemen does not do good on hope of rewards, he does not refrain from committing evil on fear of punishment, he only does what is right, because it is right.&quot;] You could say this predates state atheism by 500 years. Neo Confucianism becomes state religion/philosophy, and other thoughts are considered heretic. While studying those were not illegal, they could cause social problems and political criticisms.<br /> <br /> --------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> Next time I will be returning with culture, diplomacy, and life of women. If you have any questions, let me know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23621-tg0098","user":"tg0098","date":". 02-05-2018, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23621-tg0098","name":"tg0098","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23621_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T02:41:00-08:00","id":1182844,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\">Life in Yeomal Seoncho Era, Part 2</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Classes</span><br /> Legally, there were only two classes in both Goryeo and Joseon. Freemen and Slaves: freemen are people, slaves are treated as half-human, half-thing. Although slave's life was filled with cruelty and injustice, it wasn't atrocious as there were few heavy labor besides farming. Many peasant chose to live as slaves than suffering exploits and burdening military service. Freemen are divided into three classes: Nobles, Petty nobles/Middlemen, Commoners. Although this isn't legal division, it is cultural and influence daily lives.<br /> <br /> End of Goryeo<br /> Classes are separated firmly. Although there are some cases of exception, a noble's son will be treated as a noble whenever they go, a petty noble's power only works in his region, a commoner cannot dream of entering aristocracy. Furthermore, there are villages called Hyang, Bugok, or So(\ud5a5, \ubd80\uace1, \uc18c) that its villagers are treated as slaves from birth.<br /> <br /> Start of Joseon<br /> Although class exists, movement between classes is more fluid. Many prosperous commoners pass the National Examination final round, making their direct family noble(in Joseon Era, it is called Yangban(\uc591\ubc18)) for four generations. If noble's great-grandfather, grandfather, father, and himself do not pass the National Examination first round, they are treated as commoners. Petty nobles are stripped of their privileges and become just wealthy commoners. A new class called Middlemen emerges, they serve as experts in fields like mathematics, medicine, law, and translation. Hyang, Bugok, and So are repelled, but monks, performers, shamans, butchers are treated as slaves legally, though they have freedom.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Names</span><br /> All nobility have their names that consists of a surname with one or two(usually one) Chinese letter and a personal name consisting one or two letters, both men and women. However, a women's name is seldom mentioned out side her house. It is considered extremely rude to call someone by name. It is used only officially or by someone superior than you, like parents or king. People use Ja, an official nickname given by parents, elder relatives or teachers and Ho, an unofficial nickname given by oneself or friends.<br /> Commoners do not have surname and typically called by where they live+sequence of birth, like 'Third son of shoe seller&quot;, or they have pure Korean names, usually vulgar.<br /> A king's name is treated heavily, even using its Chinese letter is illegal, referring to king by his name is mutiny(Though it is common for kings to change their name to one exotic letter, in order to prevent inconveniences). A ruling king is called Jusang(\u4e3b\u4e0a, high lord) or Geumsang(\u4eca\u4e0a, current highness), or simply his majesty. After king dies, his subject and his successor discuss about Siho(\uc2dc\ud638, \u8ae1\u865f, Posthumous Name), and after that they are called by their posthumous name.<br /> <br /> End of Goryeo.<br /> Yuan gives Goryeo posthumous name, and forbids use of Jo and Jong, since they can be only used by independent countries. Gongmin is given by Yuan, and Gongyang is given by Joseon. Woo and Chang are their own names, since they are treated as illegitimate.<br /> <br /> Start of Joseon<br /> Taejo, Taejong, and Sejong are all names according to the siho rules. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Languages</span><br /> Both Goryeo and Joseon use Chinese character Hanja(\ud55c\uc790, \u6f22\u5b50, hanzi) since Hangeul is not yet invented(although it is soon after Yeomal Seoncho). There are two ways to write. The first is called Idu(\uc774\ub450), which borrows only sound(sometimes meaning) from Chinese characters and follows Korean grammar. Commonly used by somewhat learned commoners and Petty nobles, it is treated as a frivolity to most high nobles. The second is Hanmun(\ud55c\ubb38, \u6f22\u6587), which writes Chinese letters according to archaic Chinese literary grammar. Most commoners and slaves are illiterate, unable to read but most simple Chinese letters.<br /> Mechanically, anyone with one dot in academics could read and write Idu fluently, and can roll for understanding approximate meaning of Hanmun. Two dots in academics grants a character ability to read and write Hanmun with ease, and can roll to discover a text's authenticity, era, nationality, and style by carefully analyzing its usage of words, phrases and grammars.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Foreign Relations</span><br /> Medieval Korea's diplomatic policy is Sadaegyorin(\uc0ac\ub300\uad50\ub9b0, \u4e8b\u5927\u4ea4\u96a3), serving the powerful, befriending neighbors. Powerful means Han Chinese, although in dire situations, other &quot;barbarians&quot; like Cathay, Manchu, and Mongol could be served. One thing to note is serving does not mean Korea is China's colony. Korea, Tibet, Uighur, and Vietnam are independent countries, only accepting China's superiority(despite everything told by the current Chinese Communist Party). Neighbors mean Manchurian, Ryukyu(currently Okinawa of Japan) and Japan. Because of Yuan empire's multicultural aspect, Korea in this era has lots of contacts with places that never will be again mentioned until 19th Century. Both Goryeo and Joseon government accepts all foreigners and tries to use their abilities, but often they are faced with discrimination among the public.<br /> <br /> Foreigners that could be found in Korea without difficulty: Chinese, Japanese, Manchus, Mongolian(Until Goryeo)<br /> Foreigners that could be rarely found in Korea: Mongolian(After Joseon), Tibet, Uighur, Ryukyu.<br /> Foreigners that could or could not be existing in Korea: Turks, Ainu(now Hokkaido of Japan), Thais, Vietnamese, Champas and other Southeast Asian nationals, Arabians, Persians.<br /> Of course, European or African nationals could theoretically exist, since Marco Polo visited Yuan in 13th Century, but no known records talk about it. The first official westerner to visit Korea is Portuguese mercenaries hired by Ming in Imjin wars in 1592. And the first official westerner to live in Korea is a Dutch Jan Janesz Weltevree in 1627.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Life of Women</span><br /> Patriarchy and misogyny rules medieval days, as women are treated as second to men, and are told that their life exists to marry and nurture, and help your husband. Still, life of women is surprisingly free in this era, compared to the puritan society of late Joseon. Although women cannot become officials and are treated unequally, they could own their private property and move wherever they want. Many women expressed deep piety in Buddhism, if not outright becoming monks. They often traveling to many famous temples all by their own, something that even Buddhism-hating Joseon dynasty did not touch. Women typically have less education than men, but they still could write poems that is accepted better than her husband's, study obscure Neo Confucian texts, and debate with men equally. Many women payed much attention towards education of her young, something that has became a Korean tradition. Many books praise only mothers, not fathers for raising her sons to become loyal officials and daughters to paragon of filial piety, boasting &quot;and who fools dare to say only men contributes to the country!&quot;<br /> <br /> End of Goryeo<br /> Sexual scandals are common, although frowned upon, most of them are not punished. Divorce and remarriage is even more common than modern South Korea, noble women marrying even three or four times. A Chinese diplomat chided &quot;People of Goryeo look at marriage as if were nothing more than contracts, how pathetic.&quot; While modern perspectives view this freedom as a virtue, it has its downsides. Many women from humble families get divorced so the husband can remarry with a woman of high status. Fathers do not intervene in education and usually its up for the mother to nurture her siblings. Concubines are rare, according to Chinese texts: &quot;In Goryeo, one official tried to make concubines legal, as the word got spread, women came marching down the roads. An old hag, their leader, pointed at him and said 'there goes the old impotent who begged the king to get concubines!' The other officers were so afraid of their wives, so no more words came out on that matter.&quot;<br /> <br /> Start of Joseon<br /> Because of Neo Confucian virtues, women's freedom is restrained, although some could argue that they are more protected in return. Divorcing your wife who endured through hardship, to remarry some noble women is basically saying: &quot;Hey! Censors! Free criticism day! I don't care about my political career anymore!&quot; Early Joseon discouraged divorce without reasons among nobility. Women are free to remarry once her husband dies, and commoners do not have such restrictions. As father's, teacher's and nation's role in education is emphasized, mothers do not have the sole glory of educating their children well, but still they are praised. Concubines are treated as normal, although many nobles cannot afford one.<br /> <br /> Be creative when creating female characters. Player characters are exceptional, and there are indeed a lot of great women in this era of chaos, both traditionally and untraditionally. Supernatural society is more equal than its normal counterparts, albeit some discrimination still exists. Even when it comes to stereotypical &quot;helper of the husband&quot;, this two queens make a sharp contrast.<br /> <br /> Exceptional People -Queen Wonkyung and Queen Soheon<br /> Wonkyung is the wife of Taejong Yi Bangwon. When Taejong attempts the First strife of Princes, she ordered her family to support him, preparing weaponry and manpower. By hearing false rumor that her husband was lost, she grabbed a spear and said &quot;Rather than wait for the execution I will die fighting.&quot; It took nearly all her servants to hold her down. Once Yi Bangwon became king, she became jealous of other concubines and had a lot of fight with her husband. This only worsened after Taejong mercilessly executed her brothers, fearing they would play with the crown prince. Taejong considered divorce, but stopped by his brothers and his sons, telling him he broke her heart enough.<br /> <br /> Soheon is the wife of Sejong Yi Do. After succeeding his throne to Sejong, Taejong again purged Soheon's family. The pregnant queen was forced to watch in tears as her father was killed, and her mother made slave. Nevertheless, she helped Sejong with his many works, often acting as co-contributors, especially in Hangeul. She managed cocubines and daughters-in-law flawlessly, herself having eight sons and two daughters. Although thought by many people as passive, she commanded entire fire fighting efforts when Sejong was away, while being 9 month pregnant with her sixth son.<br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> I hope this means you now understands basic society and culture of Yeomal Sencho. If not, feel free to ask any questions. I am thinking about four example characters. What do you want to see? 1. An idealistic mage who disguised herself as eunuch to spy on her enemies. 2. A alcoholic, beggar, and martial arts master, who punishes rash mages. 3. A gisaeng who rules her &quot;entertainment company&quot; by both tyranny and generosity. 4. Middle-age Mutant Samurai Turtle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23621-tg0098","name":"tg0098","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23621_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T06:14:37-08:00","id":1183562,"title":"","content":"So, I wrote my example Leviathan character(sad that no one replied<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). I am planning to make four Leviathan characters(two pro-Goryeo, one neutral, one pro-Joseon) and four Awakened characters(one pro-Goryeo, one neutral, one pro-Joseon), and two other supernaturals. This is not a final draft, and could be changed with your ideas.<br /> <br /> <b>Hwahwa</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;We gisaengs aren't called talking flowers for no reason, Chancellor. If you wished your secrets to be secrets, why didn't you play with normal flowers instead?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> Hwahwa does not remember her original name, nor her childhood. Only thing she remembers is she was grasping on to the empty stomach when entering this Gibang. The person who brought her said she had &quot;demon-like beauty&quot; and &quot;will profit her master tenfold&quot; once she was bought. She was raised there, her master and senior Gisaengs forcing her to learn various entertainment skills, such as poetry, music, songs, dancing, and some Confucian texts by starvation and beating. Quickly enough, she showed exceptional beauty and skills, making her one of the most famous entertainers. She named herself Hwahwa, which could be interpreted as many ways, ince 'Hwa' could mean sixteen different Chinese characters.<br /> <br /> At one banquet, she had the most peculiar experience as she half-joked to one of her clients &quot;Such bravado, if you truly think I am beautiful, maybe you should buy me and make me your wife?&quot;. The client stormed out, while others, including Hwahwa herself, thought he was offended, thinking she was taunting him. But one day later, words got spread he was selling his fortunes to pay her ransom. He was stopped by his friends and relatives, but it didn't end there. Blowholes started appearing on her neck, her skin turning gray and smooth, she could hear sounds that could not be heard before. Terrified by her change, Hwahwa faked illness and refused to serve as gisaeng.<br /> <br /> But that was only the beginning. While sleeping, she was abducted by royal agents. When she woke up, she was middle of a room deep inside the palace, there she was told by invisible voices the history of Leviathans, who she is, and what she could be. And that she will marry a royal family, and will bear many fruitful Leviathan children for the dynasty. It was for her own good, they said. Would you waste your life living as some entertainer, who will likely become some whore or concubine, or become part of the noble family? Such an easy decision. To their surprise, Hwahwa managed to escape the palace after spending three nights with the hideous husband, then made her way to gibang again, this time willing.<br /> <br /> From time on, many people witnessed strange things. Her master succumbed to madness, and left Hwahwa in charge of the gibang. Many officials who visited their disappeared every few days, returning with always gleaming look on their face. Gisaengs working on her gibang asked questions lot more, a harmless curiosity appearing as innocent. Leviathans and a few others know the truth, Hwahwa is controlling entire politics. She had made many important people her beloved, and uses cultists of her to gather information that only she could wield it, which she uses to make her cult even greater. She is now meeting with Yi Sunggye and his people often, even agreeing to provide &quot;special entertainments&quot; to them. Some say she is just trying to be friendly with new powers. Others think it is not the case, and say that she hates Goryeo for everything they done to her, and will stop at nothing to its downfall.<br /> <br /> <b>Description</b>: Hwahwa is at her early twenties at the year 1388. She is strikingly beautiful, having long black hair, a curved body line, white skin. small nose and red lips. She does not make rash movements nor does she shows her emotion directly. She is both capable for acting as a coy girl unaware of her beauty, or as flirting seducer who toys men's minds. She is extremely well educated, quoting old poems and proverbs when speaking to scholars. She only attends to important banquets, but even then only provides entertainment, and will not agree to any sexual acts. To those who know her as Leviathan and master manipulator, she maintains the same attitude. Only failing her uttermost valuable plans, or confronting her with dire physical force will she show her true nature as a megalomaniac and a broken girl who seeks for revenge. Her apotheosis form is a giant dolphin. She slowly transforms from human, to somewhat slithery and gray skinned human, to a hybrid of woman and dolphin.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling hints:</b> Hwahwa is an outcast among other Leviathans, not that she cares. To the cohort that is loyal to Goryeo, she is the key person that stops united front of the Tribe. Strike her down, and anti-Goryeo Leviathans will lose their leader. Leave her alive, then she will sow discord into the Tribe, handing the throne to her new allies. To the cohort that tries to found Joseon, she is an enigmatic supporter who has her own thoughts. In truth, she is neither loyal to either of them, as she views every politician that failed to save Goryeo's people from suffering as unworthy. She plans a future that none of the pain that happen to her could happen to any other person in Korea, and to do that, she must be in control over the king. Yi Sunggye's advisors suspects this, and does not let Yi Sunggye or his sons near her. If someone crosses her path, she will first spread rumors and stories to make their social life hell, then using her cult to hunt and bring them to her, finally destroys their minds with her power, submitting them to her will.<br /> <br /> There are some things that even her iron will and master schemes do not protect her. She is indeed afraid of invisible voices from walls that once kidnapped her, leaving one door open whenever she sleeps. She feels deep connection to her gisaengs, and will act emotionally if one of them is involved. Finally, she is a poor fighter, if someone could penetrate her social defenses and henchmen, she could be easily slain in battle.<br /> <br /> <b>Story hooks:</b><br /> 1. A rumor is that Hwahwa is impregnated by one of Yi Sunggye's son. Perhaps it is the opposite, that Hwahwa impregnanted him, using her power as Leviathan. Fearing what this could mean, Jung Dojeon personally sent assassins, which all turned up dead. Now he turns to player characters, asking them to find out whether this rumor is true or false. And if possible, exterminate her.<br /> 2. One men causes a lot of commotion in front of the gibang, saying that he is heartsick of Hwahwa, asking her to meet him. Knowing this is because of the wake, Hwahwa lets him in and haves him as her cultist. But even for beloved, he is acting unusual indeed. He turns up every day, sending flowers to her(which is very rude thing to do to gisaeng, given the fact that they are called talking flowers), insulting other gisaengs for sharing her attention. Why is this happening? Hwahwa asks player characters to investigate. The answer is he is a demon who is hired by Yi Bangwon in disguise, and faking his submission to gather information.<br /> 3. When having drinks with scholars, a young men beats Hwahwa at a poetry duel, and he quickly becomes a notable person in Gaegyeong. Amused, Hwahwa tries to make him as her own beloved, but quickly discovers that he is already a beloved of a Leviathan, who is a Goryeo princess. Angered, Hwahwa plans a devious plot to snatch him from her, which is something that violates the rules of the Tribe of Korea.<br /> <br /> Upwelling: The Luerer<br /> Undertow: The Weaver<br /> Strain: Oceanid<br /> School: Sun(Dangun Hakdang)<br /> Mental Attributes: Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 3<br /> Physical Attributes: Strength 1, Dexterity 4, Stamina 2<br /> Social Attributes: Presence 4, Manipulation 4, Composure 4<br /> Mental Skills: Academics 3(Chinese History), Enigmas 2, Investigation 3, Medicine 1, Occult 3, Science 1<br /> Physical Skills: Athletics 2(Swimming), Archery 3, Brawl 1, Larceny 2, Stealth 2, Survival 1<br /> Social Skills: Animal Ken 2(Aquatic mammals), Empathy 3, Expression 4(Poetry), Intimidation 3, Persuasion 4, Socialize 3, Streetwise 3, Subterfuge 4<br /> Merits: Safe house 4(could be upgraded when 2e merits are complete), Allies(Yi Sunggye Faction) 4, Closed book 3, Contacts 3(Clients), Fame 2(Gaegyung), Pusher, Striking Looks 2, Table Turner, Professional Traning 5(Gisaeng: Academics, Expression, Empathy), Etiquette 4.<br /> Willpower: 7<br /> Sheol: 3<br /> Tranquility: 4 Divine Nature, 1 Bestial Nature.<br /> Atavisms: Ancient(Manipulation), Greater(Wits), Lesser(Dexterity and Presence)<br /> Favored Strains: Sanctity, Elements.<br /> Channels(could be changed when 2e is complete): Lambent Eyes of Judgement(Ancestral). Call of the Depths(Descendant, Song of Madness, Song of the Dolphin, Echo's of Madness), Besieging the Tower of will(Descendant, Assimilation).<br /> Cult: Thralls of the Song(Unorganized), composed of beloved clients and gisaengs. Fevor 2, Piety 4, Zeal 2.<br /> Size: 5<br /> Initiative: 8<br /> Defense: 6<br /> Speed: 10<br /> Health: 7<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> This is it. Leviathan 2e is uncompleted, but it is possible to create a character using it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23621-tg0098","user":"tg0098","date":".  Added her stat block 02-09-2018, 04:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23621-tg0098","name":"tg0098","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23621_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T06:31:06-08:00","id":1183570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Middle-age Mutant Samurai Turtle. </div> </div> </div>I was holding off any replies, waiting for this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T23:52:21-08:00","id":1184272,"title":"","content":"OK. This is an another sample character, middleage mutant samurai turtle.<br /> <br /> <b>Gwigok Gamyeong(\uf907\u8c37 \u5bb6\u660e, Kameya Ieaki)</b><br /> <i>&quot;Ilsohyeonmyung(\u4e00\u6240\u61f8\u547d), to dedicate one's life to one obligation. I prefer reciting it with my native tongue, isshokenmei.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> Gwi-gok Ga-myeong, original name Ka-me-ya Ie-aki, was born in Sakaido(now Kyushu), Japan 1351. From outside, House Kameya was known as an ordinary warrior family like any other, but in truth, they were carriers of the Bahamutan Strain, forming secluded cults. As Iekai was born, he was surrounded with worships and adoration, his family spent countless fortunes and efforts to educate and nurture him, granting him whatever the young Leviathan wants. To some, to much attention spoils the child, not for Iekai, he understood privileges comes with a heavy duty, learned literary education tirelessly, practiced hard on martial arts, and became a humble and likable person.<br /> <br /> As he grew up, Japan was getting through a Nanboku-cho Era, as there were two Tennos, each claiming that they were rightful ruler of one lineage of ten thousand years(\u4e07\u4e16\u4e00\u7cfb). Although nobles of Kyushu supported Southern dynasty, they did not waste the opportunity that Bakufu of Japan lost control of Sakaido, and many local rulers turned into pirates, pillaging Japan and other countries. Seeing no virtue in piracy, Iekai persuaded his family to refuse the order of pirating Kyoto. But they could not resist the flow of history, as Northern court attacked Kyushu and drove out Southern court sympathizers. He was forced to flee with only his body, leaving his beloved and family to die, and sailed to Tsushima(Korean name Daemado).<br /> <br /> The remnants of the Southern Courts attacked Goryeo, and Ieaki, seeing no choice but to conquer Goryeo and make it their new home, accepted reality. The Goryeo's military was weak and underfunded, its captains being corrupt and incompetent. He easily won battle after battle, and he thought their victory was near, until he met Choi Yeong. This white haired, battle-hardened general of sixties defeated the young Kameya Ieaki, and he was held captive. As Ieakai prepared for death, a women in black hood knocked his prison door, asking if he want to live. She told him a great crisis is approaching to Goryeo's Leviathans, and the Tribe could use some extra hand. Grateful that they are offering their enemy and captive an opportunity, also seeing that he had nowhere else to go, Kameya Ieaki accepted it. He is now known as Gwigok Gamyeong.<br /> <br /> There are now strange tales going on in Gaegyeong, as people are turning up dead, wounds showing they were attacked by a giant katana. The government says those are nonsense, but many people swear they saw a giant turtle leaping walls, followed by shadowy men who wield Japanese weaponry. Mages and other supernaturals who is known to be pro-Yi Sunggye, or those who knows to oppose the regime will be visited by Gamyeong and his cult. He has failed to save one dynasty, and he will not fail to save another.<br /> <br /> <b>Description</b>: Gwigok Gamyeong dresses like ordinary Korean to prevent hassle, and it is difficult to distinguish him as Japanese without a detailed look(only for Koreans, as they will say &quot;I dunno, but something about him doesn't look Korean&quot;). A decent looking man in his late thirties, he is a quiet person who does not show his abilities nor his knowledge without being asked. His answers are often polite but short. His Korean is fluent enough, but he has an undeniable Japanese accent(a Miami accent could be fitting for English users). When questioned he does not deny he is Japanese, saying he is deeply moved by the nation's generosity to him, and expresses his deep loyalty to Goryeo. He lives in a mansion, which belongs to the royal family just outside Gaegyung. He practices calligraphy and swordsmanship there, and some of his beloved living there as well. When carrying out a mission from the Tribe, he dresses in black Korean clothes, but wields his heirloom katana. His apotheosis is a giant leatherback sea turtle, his hybrid form looking like the protagonists of 'Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling hints:</b> Gwigok Gamyeong is the fist of the Tribe. When there is order for execution, he carries out the mission. When dire threat approaches, he is sent to slay it. A combat pragmatist and trained tactician before the time of Bushido, he uses various methods to get victory, using traps, deception and surprise attacks. Although he will refrain from killing the surrendered, children, Buddhist monks, and members of the Tribe, he will do so if it seems necessary. He complements his mediocre talents by his rigorous training and almost inhuman feats.<br /> To the pro-Goryeo Player Characters, he is a valuable ally and a key asset, who is devoted to Goryeo dynasty to the almost point of selflessness. To the pro-Joseon Player Characters, he is the last supernatural bodyguard of the Goryeo dynasty, eliminating him will mean they could use violence to get what they want. If Gamyeong thinks someone could threaten the Goryeo dynasty, he first visits them and sends out his warning in well-mannered way. Second time, he uses his cult to cause the mood of fear and anxiety over them. If they still do not back down, he will attack them personally.<br /> <br /> There are few ways to put Gwigok in corner. First, his Japanese ethnicity arouses suspicion and fear among Koreans, even to the Tribe. It is only magnified to the fact his cult contains of many surrendered Waegus. Using it could put him in dangerous situations, fabricating or finding some evidence could launch an official execution order. Second, Japanese pirates are still out there, and many consider Gamyeong as a traitor to their own kind, and it could cause serious trouble in his cult. Finally, defeating in battle could count, but he is a fearful foe even when attacked in surprise, and can endure damage by his power as a Bahamutan. When cornered in his own house, he will wear full Japanese battle armor and will wield multiple weapons, fighting until death.<br /> <br /> <b>Story hooks:</b><br /> 1. A merchant claims he met a Japanese who claims he is the last remaining Tenno of the Southern dynasty. Could this be true? Why he is in Korea? Nevertheless, the Tribe secretly tells the Cohort to eliminate the so called Tenno, since it could waver Gamyeong's loyalty to Goryeo. But if Gamyeong learns about this, the betrayal will surely make him reconsider his allegiance. What do the Cohort do?<br /> 2. Gamyeong is very proud of his katana Gyakuchou(\u9006\u6f6e, \uc5ed\uc870, Yeokjo, Riptide), which is a heirloom of House Kameya. Yi Sunggye faction knows about this, and sends an envoy claiming Yi Sunggye has a relic sword, which will be later called Jeon-eodo(\uc804\uc5b4\ub3c4, \u50b3\u5fa1\u5200, king-used blade.), and asks Gwigok Gamyeong to examine each other's swords. Gwigok suspects this could be a trap, but claiming such suspicion openly or refusing the offer without proper reason is a poor etiquette. He asks the Player Characters to investigate about it.<br /> 3. Gamyeong's calligraphy is famous among Gaegyung, people asking him to write something they want. Then a mysterious person appears, has a look at his works, and claims &quot;you can see mutiny in those letters.&quot; And uses bizarre historic and literary knowledge to put Gamyeong in a very bad position. Who is that person?<br /> <br /> Upwelling: The Reedemer<br /> Undertow: The Savage<br /> Strain: Bahamutan<br /> School: Fog(Murim Hakdang)<br /> Mental Attributes: Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> Physical Attributes: Strength 3, Dexterity 2, Stamina 5<br /> Social Attributes: Presence 2, Manipulation 1, Composure 4<br /> Mental Skills: Academics 3, Enigmas 1, Investigation 1, Medicine 1, Occult 3, Politics 2<br /> Physical Skills: Athletics 4(Swimming), Archery 3, Brawl 3, Stealth 4, Survival 2, Riding 2, Weaponry 5(katana)<br /> Social Skills: Empathy 3, Expression 3(Caligraphy), Intimidation 1, Persuasion 1, Socialize 2, Streetwise 2<br /> Merits: Danger Sense, Language(Korean), Quick Draw, Safe house 2(could be upgraded when 2e merits are complete), Allies(Tribe) 2, Fame 1(Gaegyung), Heirloom 4(Gyakuchou, always match the size of the owner even if they are enlarged by transformation), Defensive Combatant(Weaponry), Killer Instinct, Style:Heavy Weaponry 5.<br /> Willpower: 7<br /> Sheol: 2<br /> Tranquility: 1 Divine Nature, 2 Bestial Nature.<br /> Atavisms: Ancient(Stamina), Greater(Wits), Lesser(Dexterity)<br /> Favored Strains: Vitality, Might.<br /> Channels(could be changed when 2e is complete): Flesh of the Progenitors(Ancestral)<br /> Cult: Converted of the Yamato(Militant Fanatics), which is mostly consisted of converted Waegus. Fervor 3, Piety 1, Zeal 1 <br /> Size: 5<br /> Initiative: 6<br /> Defense: 7<br /> Speed: 10<br /> Health: 10<br /> Armor: 0/0(if armored, 2/0)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23621-tg0098","name":"tg0098","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23621_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T22:51:10-08:00","id":1184637,"title":"","content":"Just had a better look at the two characters. I honestly don't know enough about Leviathan, so I can't say much on their stats... but otherwise the concepts look pretty solid.<br /> <br /> And I've just noticed that both of them are of the &quot;lower class,&quot; so to speak, in the country. Surprising, since my mental image of leviathans have them being the barons and princes of their territory. (Yes, the characters exert greater-than-seeming influence, especially Hwahwa, and they do have their cults, but still) Was it intentional design, or happenstance?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T01:07:26-08:00","id":1184657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1181363-fanmade-dark-era-leviathan-mage-entwined-dragons?p=1184637#post1184637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I've just noticed that both of them are of the &quot;lower class,&quot; so to speak, in the country. Surprising, since my mental image of leviathans have them being the barons and princes of their territory. (Yes, the characters exert greater-than-seeming influence, especially Hwahwa, and they do have their cults, but still) Was it intentional design, or happenstance?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It was just happenstance. The next Leviathan character would be one of Goryeo's royal family, she is mentioned on both Hwahwa and Gamyeong's backstory. The fourth character will be a very novice Leviathan from a local landlord family who just learned about the tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23621-tg0098","name":"tg0098","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23621_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T02:42:24-08:00","id":1185525,"title":"","content":"This is my third example Leviathan, who is the current leader of the Korean Tribe.<br /> <br /> <b>Princess Hyonyeong</b><br /> <i>&quot;Goryeo is my home. It never had been a good home to me, and you will not see me admitting I have many happy memories of it. But still, Goryeo is my one and only home.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> Princess Hyo-nyeong(which is a title, not a name.) was born in as a daughter of king Chunghye. Her father was a reveler whose hobby was to rape relatives and subjects' wives. His lascivious acts continued to the point his subjects asked the Yuan Emperor for permission to change the king. After her father was dethroned, young Hyonyeong watched her sister Jangnyeong sent to Yuan to marry their prince, her two elder brothers take the throne but both surviving less than five years. Although the successor Gongmin ruled fair and square, Hyonyeong always had a piece of fear whenever she saw him. In the small room at the deepest palace she submitted herself to books, reading history and scripture fervently.<br /> <br /> One day, she found a ragged text which contained the history of Goryeo's foundation. It was marked [restricted] by the seal of Yuan inspectors. Out of curiosity, she ripped the seal and looked at the contents. What wonder she found! Story of Wang Gun, who was a son of Wang Ryung the master merchant of the west sea, and a grandson of a great pirate Jak Jegeon who brought fear in the entire ocean. Legacy of the Founder, who sailed behind his enemies lines and surprise attacked them from behind, creating a secondary battlefront. Best of all, they could do that because they were more than human. They were Leviathans.<br /> <br /> As Hyonyeong learned about this, her heart surged with great pride. It was only weeks after she entered the metamorphosis. She quickly learned that Gongmin was a Leviathan too, and her feeling of fear is just a mask for territory instinct. She experimented with her powers and tried to improve her cult. It is unsurprising that she gained great respect of the Tribe, both by her heritage and her skills. Hyonyeong was the first to warn the Tribe of Gongmin's madness, the first to notice dark clouds spreading over the Tribe, and the first to take action about it. She gathered Leviathan, Lahmasu, and mortal allies by persuasion, lies, and force. Gongmin's death shook her, and as she inherited the role of the sole leader of the Tribe from Gongmin, the more and more brutal and manipulative she became.<br /> <br /> Now, the Tribe is beginning to worry she might turn into Ophion or Typhon, but none addresses such fears out loud. Hyonyeong knows that Yi Sunggye is the would-be usurper, and she will destroy anyone, including the Leviathans, who dares to slow her attacks. At one gathering, she cried out loud there is no such thing as neutrality. You are either with her, the Tribe, the Goryeo dynasty, the true Confucian way, or you are with the heretical enemy.<br /> <br /> <b>Description</b>: Princess Hyonyeong is a woman of late forties. She is unmarried and has no plans for doing so. Even by just her looks, she spread the aura of majesty and charisma. In mortal society, she resides in her mansion, but frequently gets visits from nobles, scholars, and monks. She appears to be generous and tolerant, giving large gifts to all her visitors and listening to thoughts that do not match with her ideas. But she views them nothing more as chess pieces to move and will not hide it to fellow Leviathans. To the Tribe, she acts like a dictator who thinks herself as a necessary evil. She will not accept disobeys from fellow Leviathans, and will demonstrate her martial and social prowess to her opposition. She is possesses almost absolute knowledge thanks to her channels, cults and contacts. Her apotheosis is a giant sea serpent.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling hints:</b> There are few, if any things that Hyonyeong will hesitate to sacrifice for Goryeo. As a confucian, she understands that Goryeo needs reforms, but also is aware that those reforms could be used by Yi Sunggye faction to gain influence. Being the matriarch of the whole(well, at least nearly whole, since some Leviathans like hwahwa do not accept her as their leader) she wields immense power both in mortal and supernatural societies. Those who oppose her will have to prepare for countless attacks from famed scholars, ambushes by assassins, and direct attacks by veteran members of the Tribe. To the pro-Goryeo player characters, she is a dictator that needs to survive, since there are no members of the Tribe that could handle such gargantuan task. She could act as a unreliable mentor or helper to them, although asking her help for poor reasons(ex. We are too weak for them!) will only infuriate her. To the pro-Joseon players, she could act as a 'final boss' to the chronicle if you are going to finish your story by the creation of Joseon.<br /> <br /> She does look invincible, but there are ways. Many Leviathans have discontent with her rule, and a skilled diplomat could persuade them for open treason. Her position as a princess also restricts her somewhat, so she mostly relies on her mortal acquaintances for social influence. Making them convert or threatening them will make her lose core assets in protecting Goryeo. Finally, her cult is a secret society, so exposing them could land her(and the entire Goryeo royal family) in a very bad position. As for comabt, she is a skilled fighter, and defeating her in battle will be difficult.<br /> <br /> <b>Story hooks:</b><br /> 1. Hyonyeong makes a renowned scholar into her beloved. His pupils became suspicious of their master's behavior and begins to investigate. They find out about their master is meeting with the princess regularly, and openly accuses them of adultery. Yi Sunggye faction asks for investigation to the scholar. Although they did not yet turn the arrow to Hyonyeong, it is only matter of time. Hyonyeong is in surveillance, so the Tribe cannot contact her. What should they do?<br /> 2. Although never had been married, Hyonyeong has some secret children, both born or sired. One of those son is a Lahmasu who killed a civilian by accident. Hyonyeong herself executes a kill order to the Player Characters. When confronted, he pleads to the PCs, asking them to let him see his mother for once and for all. Should they accept it? If they agree, he will be killed by Hyonyeong herself the second he enters the palace, if they let him hide, Gwigok Gamyeong will be sent to hunt them.<br /> 3. A masked men turns dead at a riverside. The players character investigates this, and learns that he belongs to Hyonyeong's cult Muyeong-Gongheo(None zero, Null void). Luckily, he had some secret codes and the date of the next meeting. If they disguise as cultists and infiltrate the gathering, they could earn hidden information about Hyonyeong.<br /> <br /> Upwelling: The Patriarch<br /> Undertow: The Fury<br /> Strain: Tannim<br /> School: Bamboo(Juja Hakdang)<br /> Mental Attributes: Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 3<br /> Physical Attributes: Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 4<br /> Social Attributes: Presence 5, Manipulation 3, Composure 2<br /> Mental Skills: Academics 3, Enigmas 4, Investigation 3, Occult 4, Politics 3, Science 1<br /> Physical Skills: Athletics 3(Swimming), Archery 2, Brawl 3, Riding 2, Weaponry 3<br /> Social Skills: Empathy 2, Expression 2, Intimidation 4, Persuasion 2, Socialize 2, Subefuge 2<br /> Merits: Safe house 4(could be upgraded when 2e merits are complete), Allies(Tribe) 5, Fame 2(Gaegyung), Recourse 4, Status(Nobility) 5, Contacts 3(Royal family), Lahmasu Cult merit<br /> Willpower: 5<br /> Sheol: 5<br /> Tranquility: 5 Divine Nature, 4 Bestial Nature.<br /> Atavisms: Ancient(Stamina), Greater(Wits), Lesser(Dexterity)<br /> Favored Strains: Predation, Awarness<br /> Channels(could be changed when 2e is complete): Lambent Eyes of Judgement(Ancestral, Pyre for Sinners), The Key and the Gate(Descendant), Eye of the Deity(Descendant, All-seeing, Gentle touch), King atop the Bloody throne(Ancestral, Alpha, Kneel before Zod), Mortal Devouring Armory(Ancestral)<br /> Cult: Muyeong Gongheo(People from various backgrounds, Secret Society), Fervor 4, Piety 5, Zeal 4<br /> Size: 5<br /> Initiative: 5<br /> Defense: 6<br /> Speed: 11<br /> Health: 9<br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> Princess Hyonyeong is a fictional character. The only known daughter of Chunghye is Jangnyeong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23621-tg0098","name":"tg0098","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23621_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T05:17:24-08:00","id":1188138,"title":"","content":"This is my final example Leviathan. He roughly has the same power level as the starting Player Characters, and can be played as a premade Player Character when playing 1 on 1. Sorry for the long delay.<br /> <br /> <b>Kim Cheongsu</b><br /> <i>&quot;OK... I get that I'm a half-god, half-monster from ancient sea that fucks with people's minds. So... what now?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> As a landlord's son born in Andong, Kim Cheongsu had little worries. Sure, he didn't have much interest in academics so fame and honor were something he could never have, he had a lot of brothers and sisters which could cause(and has caused in his upper generation) inheritance disputes, but he didn't want much. He liked going out and enjoying mountains and river, resting at a tree near his family's mansion, hearing strange tales and interesting news told by monks, elders and wanderers. His family didn't expect much from him either, and was even pleased that he will not participate in infighting of the sibilings. To Cheongsu, everything was completely fine until the metamorphosis began.<br /> <br /> His eyes occasionally bulged out like an angler fish, which was also resembled by sprouting lantern on his forehead whenever he woke up. Deformed squirrels and rabbits began to following him, and his slaves would instinctively react to his very thoughts. Panicked by this transformation, he gathered every bits of information he could find, until he heard from a village elder that long time ago, a women from the seacoast married his great-great grandfather, who had the exactly the same condition as Cheongsu. And that his favorite tree was planted only a year after their wedding. Shocked at this information, he shoveled the tree that night.<br /> <br /> What he found was something that he still has difficulty expressing it. Hundreds of infant skeletons, each having deformed skulls or bones, were buried near the tree. While he stood still, stunned that his family had so many deformed stillbirths, he was surrounded by his relatives. They claimed this bloodline was a curse which should be kept secret from the outsiders, and must be exterminated, and said &quot;We're sorry, but you bear that curse more than any of us. Goodbye.&quot; As he was brutally assaulted, Cheongsu managed to transform and crept to the river, blacking out almost he touched the water, letting the flow consume him.<br /> <br /> When he woke up, he found himself bandaged and cured by a woman with brown skin and exotic face. She introduced herself as Rania, a hermit from Arabia who dwells in a cave near the river. She refused to tell further, but her care and medicine was enough to make him regain his strength. Not knowing what to do next, he spent some time with Rania in her den, and found that he enjoyed her company with her surprisingly vast and insightful knowledge, caring and humble character. But that did not last long as his relatives discovered their hiding place, forcing them to flee. Now Cheongsu wanders the whole country with Rania as his company, his destination Gaegyung. Although that does not stop him from detouring to famous scenic spots.<br /> <br /> <b>Description</b>: Kim Cheongsu is only a teenager, while he is accepted as a legal adult, culturally he is still a minor. He has more than average looks and physique, but anyone looking at him will instantly now he is far from a trained body. He talks with a heavy Yeongnam-reigion accent and is not familiar with the aristocratic customs of the central nobility. He is often clumsy and distracted, but make this up by his sense of humor and enthusiasm. He learned from Rania the basic history and abilities of the Leviathan and is keen to explore it. But he has almost no information of the current Tribe, and the Player Characters will most likely be the first other Leviathans he will meet. He is fairly attracted to Rania, but will not admit it out loud, thinking she is so better than him.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling hints:</b> Rania is a powerful Promethean who entered Goryeo four hundred years ago, and Cheongsu does not know this. Learning her true nature will shake him hard. Except from this secret, he is an ideal friend to both pro-Goryeo and pro-Joseon Cohort. Just following him and Rania to Gaegyung, and learning about the problems and issues of current Korea could be good first phase of the Chronicle. Otherwise, trying to recruit him for PC's faction could be a good mission to a newly fledged Cohort. Cheongsu understands that big houses like his family in Andong are the plague that corrode Goryeo, but is reluctant at the idea of founding a new nation. He will be fairly moderate even when after joining a faction.<br /> <br /> It is hard to turn him as an enemy, but even if you did, he himself is nothing to fear. He has little fighting skills, have few contacts outside his hometown and his cult is disorganized. He has roughly the power of one starting character, and cannot stand the might of the entire cohort on his own. Kim Cheongsu knows this too, and he will try to flee, but if things get dangerous he will try to save Rania because of his debt to her and his chivalry. Of course, whether the Tribe can take on the 400-year-old Promethean, that is an entirely different matter.<br /> <br /> <b>Story hooks:</b><br /> 1. It is well known that Divine Fire and Primordial Waters do not mix well. As Cheongsu develops his powers, those two opposing forces clash with all their might. Almost everyone around him, including his Beloved, go insane. Rania quickly realizes this is appearing because she broke her role when coming out from that den. She disappears without leaving a message. Cheongsu asks the Player Characters to aid in his search for her.<br /> 2. The Kim Clan of Andong is a traditional and powerful family. Although Cheongsu's family was only their small branch, the head of the eldest branch learns about his escape, and sends a message to him saying he will arrange a &quot;make-up meeting&quot; with his family. Because this is an offer from the Clan's leader, refusing it will cause a major commotion. Cheongsu accepts this, but asks the Tribe some reliable bodyguards for the rendezvous.<br /> 3. Before arriving at Gaegyung, Cheongsu wants to go for the Geumgang mountain, which is the most famous tourism site in the Goryeo dynasty(and still are, at least in the North Korea). The problem is it is the territory of the elder Tannim turned into Typhon, who dwells in the nine-dragon falls. She will lash out at the party if they approach near her.<br /> <br /> Upwelling: The Watcher<br /> Undertow: The Hoarder<br /> Strain: Dagon<br /> School: Reef(Murim Hakdang)<br /> Mental Attributes: Intelligence 1, Wits 3, Resolve 2<br /> Physical Attributes: Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 2<br /> Social Attributes: Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 2<br /> Mental Skills: Academics 1, Investigation 2, Occult 2(Folktales), Politics 2<br /> Physical Skills: Athletics 1(Swimming), Archery 1, Brawl 1, Stealth 1<br /> Social Skills: Empathy 2, Expression 1, Persuasion 3, Socialize 3(Humor), Subefuge 2<br /> Merits: True Friend(Rania), Danger Sense, Narrow Wake<br /> Willpower: 4<br /> Sheol: 1<br /> Tranquility: 1 Divine Nature, 1 Bestial Nature.<br /> Atavisms: Ancient(Presence), Greater(Resolve), Lesser(Dexterity)<br /> Favored Strains: Fecundity, Sanctity<br /> Channels(could be changed when 2e is complete): Hydra's Rebirth(Descendant, Blessings of the Chirurgeon God), Piercing the Veil of Slumber(Descendant)<br /> Cult: Aqua Tourists(Unorganized), composed of strays he met along the way. Fevor 1, Piety 3, Zeal 0 <br /> Size: 5<br /> Initiative: 5<br /> Defense: 4<br /> Speed: 10<br /> Health: 7<br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> So, this is it. The concept is the &quot;supernatural but unaware boy meets the powerful supernatural girl&quot; from various animes. Rania will be shown as the sample other supernaturals. What do you think I should do now? Make some unique mechanics? Introduce some historical figures? Add more detail to the Leviathan/Mage society? Just let me know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23621-tg0098","name":"tg0098","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23621_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T14:54:41-08:00","id":1188310,"title":"","content":"Normally I\u2019d vote for unique mechanics... but since I probably can\u2019t recognize what\u2019s unique and not in Leviathan 2E, I suggest Wicked &amp; Awakened society.<br /> <br /> Do they largely do their separate things, as much supernaturals did in most other Dark Eras, or do they have some working relationship like mummies and immortals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T01:35:08-08:00","id":1188436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1181363-fanmade-dark-era-leviathan-mage-entwined-dragons?p=1188310#post1188310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Normally I\u2019d vote for unique mechanics... but since I probably can\u2019t recognize what\u2019s unique and not in Leviathan 2E, I suggest Wicked &amp; Awakened society.<br /> <br /> Do they largely do their separate things, as much supernaturals did in most other Dark Eras, or do they have some working relationship like mummies and immortals?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They normally do their own things, but because the Earth's most Wicked Tribe's official stance is protecting Goryeo, and many Awakened are keen to build a new nation, they often view each other as enemies in this era. That is the one reason I did not emphasize the Marduk Society/Seers of the Throne in this era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23621-tg0098","name":"tg0098","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23621_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T02:49:58-07:00","id":1237921,"title":"","content":"Status Update: Sorry for the long delay. I got conscripted to the ROK Army(Thanks, Kim Jeong Un!). So I think this delay will get much longer, since in military, it's hard for me to find time to write long stuff on the internet. I'll try to find some ways. It will be very grateful for me if some of you could contribute on this project.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23621-tg0098","name":"tg0098","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23621_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T06:09:55-07:00","id":1239268,"title":"","content":"Saw this just now; for those unaware, this means he\u2019ll hardly have free time for two years or so. Mandatorily conscripted soldiers in South Korea are government-approved second-class citizens all but in name - no patriotic glory of serving the homeland here. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile; damn I should\u2019ve studied up my country\u2019s history more. Rare occasion where I actually want to study History on my own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T04:34:04-08:00","id":1358827,"title":"","content":"Finally! I'm out of the military and ready to complete this task. Current plan is creating 4 more example Mage characters + Homebrew politics rule + 2 other Supernatural characters. If there is anything you want to see first, let me know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23621-tg0098","name":"tg0098","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23621_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T01:43:44-07:00","id":1377687,"title":"","content":"I am finally getting into Leviathan so I'm bumping this as I look into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}